# Database

## Engine

PostgreSQL 16. Connection via `pg.Pool` with `DATABASE_URL` env var.

## Naming

- Tables: `snake_case` plural (`bookings`, `services`, `content_blocks`, `users`)
- Columns: `snake_case` (`user_name`, `created_at`, `is_active`)
- Primary keys: `id UUID DEFAULT gen_random_uuid()`
- Timestamps: `created_at TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT now()`, `updated_at TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT now()`
- Multilingual columns: `title_ru`, `title_en`, `title_am` pattern

## Migrations

Plain SQL files in `server/migrations/`, sorted by filename (prefix with `NNN_`). Tracked via `_migrations` table. Run with `npm run migrate -w server`. Each migration runs inside a single transaction.

## Queries

No ORM. Raw parameterized SQL via `query(text, params)`. Build dynamic WHERE clauses with positional `$N` params. Never concatenate user input into SQL strings.

## Soft Deletes

Services use soft-delete (`is_active = FALSE`). Bookings use status-based lifecycle (`new` -> `in_progress` -> `completed`/`cancelled`).
